      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}  It can SOMETIMES make sense if you have hair strands of differing lengths that need different properties, or don't need collision (eg;  long hair with bangs doesn't need collision on the bangs, just the long back strands), but like 99% of the time it's dumb and you should totally just put a single physbone on the root bone to control it all.  \n\nPlus you can set physbones that override OTHER physbones on same transforms, and just control those differing bone strands on their own.  (ie;  Just put a physbone on the root of a strand under the main physbone and set it to override it).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
